                                "sense_id": "a400e2ed-035f-3a8e-816a-dc8273b948d2",
                                "text": "Only certain epithets and metaphors were authorized; themes were similarly restricted, metres fixed, and Cynghanedd, the repetitive use of consonantal sequences with variation of vowels, became a burdensome obsession."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e09ed58-ab4e-44cf-8e33-fdaead571713",
                                "sense_id": "a400e2ed-035f-3a8e-816a-dc8273b948d2",
                                "text": "1998, editors (names unknown), \"cynghanedd\" in Britannica Online Encyclopedia\nThere are four fundamental types of cynghanedd, but within these there are a number of refinements and variations. When skillfully used, cynghanedd is capable of conveying an almost unlimited variety of subtle effects."
